#N Puffer 1
#O Bill Gosper, 1971
#C explanation: The first pattern found that moves and leaves something behind. Two
#C explanation: lightweight spaceships tow an unstable centre that sheds a repeating trail
#C explanation: of blocks and blinkers every 128 generations. Before this, moving objects
#C explanation: kept their cells and stationary ones stayed put; a puffer does neither, and
#C explanation: it opened the way to patterns whose population grows without limit.
